Copy the package and then work. Make sure folder structure is same for smooth flow.


1. Make the terminal tcsh
2. Source the tool cshrc file
3. Update "sourceme_first" with proper paths in your work area and then source it in terminal.
4. Inside each of syn/ pnr/user_files and pt/, update the user_defines.tcl properly

Synthesis Step
5. Go to syn folder
6. run the following in terminal
   dc_shell -f synthesize_simple.tcl | tee syn.log
The synthesized verilog file is saved in appropriate location

PNR Step
7. Go to pnr folder
8. Launch innovus, then source scripts/top.tcl

PT(PrimeTime) Step
9. Go to pt folder
10 run the following command in terminal
   pt_shell -f pt_simple.tcl | tee pt.log
11. Review the log file for basic setup timing and average power analysis results



NOTES
1. Do not just blindly run the flow. Understand each step and each command, explore more possible options and commands.
2. Learn to interpret the reports as needed. The various QoR (Quality of Results) metric should be summarized by you after the full flow.
